      "writtenOn": "2026-03-05T02:13:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This part is different in 6.12 which didn\u0027t have early reservation support. `count` here represents the memory that was reserved during early reservation [cmr-\u003ebase_pfn, early_pfn] and the area we need to initialize is [early_pfn, cmr-\u003ebase_pfn + cmr-\u003ecount]. So, the size of the area that needs to be initialized is (cmr-\u003ecount - count). That\u0027s why I set it to 0 if early_pfn[r] \u003d\u003d cmr-\u003ebase_pfn, IOW if there was no early reservation and we need to initialize the whole area. Later on `count` is used in register_gcma_area() call.",
      "parentUuid": "fdf01d85_59cbeae7",
